# Lick: Bends in Tune (repertoire plan: st-lick-bend). An original 8-bar lick in A minor
# pentatonic box 1 over a slow minor groove: Am7 Am7 | Dm7 Dm7 | Am7 Am7 | E7 | Am7.
# Every bend is set up by its target: first play the fret you are aiming for, then bend up to the
# same pitch, then (bars 1 and 3) hear the target once more on the next string as a check.
#   D on string 3 fret 7, bent a whole step to E (the pitch of string 3 fret 9): bars 1 and 5;
#   G on string 2 fret 8, bent a whole step to A (the pitch of string 2 fret 10): bars 3 and 6;
#   G on string 2 fret 8, bent a half step to G# (the pitch of string 2 fret 9) over E7: bar 7.
# Bend with finger 3, with fingers 1 and 2 on the same string behind it, pushing together. Play
# the target note with finger 3 too (finger 4 for G# at fret 9), so the hand learns the distance.
title: Lick: Bends in Tune
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original lick in A minor pentatonic, box 1
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: bend, minor pentatonic, box 1, lick, blues
tempo: 72
time: 4/4
key: Am

track: Your lick
role: lead
[Whole step: D to E]
| "Am7=x02010" ^"target E" q 3:9{3} ^"bend D up to E" h 3:7b{3} q 2:5{1} | e 2:8{4} 2:5{1} 3:7{3} 3:5{1} h 4:7{3} |
[Whole step: G to A]
| "Dm7=xx0211" ^"target A" q 2:10{3} ^"bend G up to A" h 2:8b{3} q 1:5{1} | e 1:8{4} 1:5{1} 2:8{4} 2:5{1} h 3:7{3} |
[Both bends]
| "Am7" q 3:9{3} 3:7b{3} e 2:5{1} 2:8{4} q 1:5{1} | q 2:10{3} 2:8b{3} e 2:5{1} 3:7{3} q 3:5{1} |
[Half step over E7]
| "E7=020100" ^"target G#" q 2:9{4} ^"half-step bend" h 2:8b1{3} e 2:5{1} 3:7{3} | "Am7" q 3:5{1} e 4:7{3} 4:5{1} h 4:7{3} ||

